- **The formula's two halves, READ by the drafter (rows h3, h4 — measure):** (i) `Math.min(5000, deadline - Date.now())` — H1's deadline is 3000 ms, so a
  mutant with a FLAT `AbortSignal.timeout(5000)` aborts at ~5 s, fails the boot at ~5.1 s, and H1's `< 8000` still holds: **predicted H1 GREEN — the
  "bounded by the boot deadline" half is guarded by no cell**; (ii) `Math.max(250, …)` — without it, an iteration that starts after the deadline passed
