  directories only. Earlier gates' trees are their evidence — copy from, never run in.
- `node_modules`: an APFS clone (`cp -c -R`) of the newest gate tree you trust, **after proving** `package-lock.json` is blob `9064763` there too; a real
  directory, never a symlink.

## 2. Why these tiers, and who is waiting
- **RD-648 TIER 2:** test harness only. **A boot that still holds `bootServer` (and so the jest lock) past its deadline plus a bounded margin is a Major
  (the RD-619 class the ticket exists to close); a consumer that PASSED at M0 and fails (or turns flaky) on the merged tree is a Major; a consumer that
  was RED at M0 and turns GREEN is a Major until explained (an abort must never mask a failure); an unguarded half of the formula is a Minor (C-40);
  a leaked child or temp directory is a Minor/Polish.**
- **RD-609 TIER 2:** **a tree kind in which a cell PASSES having checked nothing is a Major (F-7's own class); a malformed row reported by nothing is a
  Minor (row p4); a C-57 comparison that loses an id silently is a STOP; wording is Polish.**
- **RD-700 TIER 2:** **any executable change in the rd411 file is a Major AND a WRONG item** (the commission's condition); **a comment that states
  something false about the code or its history is a Minor**; wording is Polish.
- **Who is waiting:** the merge author for all three is **NexusAI-N (S86N)**, lane 2, under C-184/C-186's turn order (O, P, M, N).

